# Claude Code
CLAUDE.local.md

# Per-project data (runtime databases, sessions, worktrees)
.kangentic/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
kangentic.local.json

# Local dev rig state (relay repo path, stub phone key, AVD override)
.devrig.local.json
# Runtime pid records written by scripts/dev.mjs so it only ever stops processes
# it started. Machine-local state, and the recorded `commandLine` can contain a
# developer's home directory, which must not land in a public repo
# (.claude/rules/no-personal-info.md).
.devrig-processes/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.npm

# Expo / React Native
.expo/
.expo-shared/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*

# Native projects are generated by `npx expo prebuild` (Continuous Native
# Generation). Never hand-edit or commit them - see
# .claude/rules/expo-cng.md.
/ios/
/android/

# EAS / secrets - never commit credentials or environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
# Sentry CLI config. Both can carry an auth token (org-scoped, able to
# upload releases and read issues) and neither matched any glob above.
# `sentry-cli login` writes ~/.sentryclirc outside the repo, but the CLI
# also reads a project-local copy, and the config plugin can generate a
# sentry.properties into the native projects.
.sentryclirc
sentry.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
secrets/
*service-account*.json
# Anything keystore-shaped, not just the binary. A file holding the store/key
# passwords, or a base64 copy of the .jks (from which the keystore is fully
# reconstructible), is exactly as sensitive as the keystore itself and matched
# none of the globs above.
*keystore*
# Defensive: the real credentials live OUTSIDE this repo (see the Android release
# section of docs/developer-guide.md). This only exists so that copying that
# folder in by accident cannot become a commit.
kangentic-secrets/
#
# KNOWN GAP, do not rely on this list alone: Google Cloud names downloaded
# service-account keys `<project>-<hash>.json`, which matches none of these
# patterns unless the file is renamed to contain "service-account". Filename
# globs are inherently leaky, so the real backstop is GitHub secret scanning with
# push protection, enabled on this repo, which matches on content instead.

# Local native build outputs (EAS builds run in the cloud; local builds drop these)
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

# Logs
/logs/
*.log

